{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":285327,"duration_api_ms":285268,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge in observable behavior. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build/generation targets). Human operator writes PRDs; orchestrator generates Go code.\n\n**Implementation status**: Specs exist for testutils, sys, format, ts, wc, cat, sponge, du, and ls. Generated code (4,586 LOC) exists at generation-merged tags but not on the working branch. All packages show codestatus \"not started\" on this branch.\n\n**Current release scope**: Release 04.0 — \"Batch 4 — ls core specification and differential test\" with use case `rel04.0-uc001-ls` (spec_complete, code not started).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 04.0 has a single use case (`rel04.0-uc001-ls`) with spec_complete status and no code. The task is to implement the core ls utility. Per P2, implementation and tests are split — with only 1 task allowed, the implementation task takes priority (P8: implementation before tests). The ls core implementation depends on `pkg/sys/` and `pkg/format/` interfaces; the stitch agent will read those packages from required_reading.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/ls core implementation -- entry point, flag parsing, directory listing, and output (rel04.0-uc001-ls)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure, pkg/sys/ and pkg/format/ interfaces, design decisions DD3 and DD6)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find and read the ls PRD -- file matching prd*-ls*.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.0-uc001-ls.yaml (ls core use case flow)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-04.0.yaml (expected ls core behaviors and test inputs)\n      - pkg/sys/ (file metadata interfaces -- stat, lstat, terminal size detection)\n      - pkg/format/ (column alignment and ANSI color interfaces)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Core ls implementation: entry point, flag parsing, directory reading, sorting, and output formatting\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement the main entry point with flag parsing for ls core flags as specified in the ls PRD. Parse command-line arguments to distinguish flags from file/directory operands. Default to current directory when no operands are given.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement directory entry reading and metadata collection. Open each operand, read directory entries, collect file metadata via pkg/sys stat/lstat. Sort entries alphabetically in LC_ALL=C byte order by default.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement output formatting for default mode (one-per-line when stdout is not a terminal, multi-column when stdout is a terminal) and long format (-l) using pkg/format for column alignment. Long format includes file type, permissions, link count, owner, group, size, and modification time.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement exit code handling per the ls PRD -- exit 0 on success, exit 1 on minor problems (cannot access a named file), exit 2 on serious errors. Report errors to stderr without aborting processing of remaining operands.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/sys for all stat/lstat calls and terminal detection per ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD3. Do not import golang.org/x/sys directly in cmd/ls/.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/format for column alignment in long-format and multi-column output per ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD3.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All string comparison and sorting uses LC_ALL=C byte-order semantics per ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD6. Do not implement locale-aware collation.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Follow the cmd/ package structure from ARCHITECTURE.yaml -- single package cmd/ls with main.go as the primary implementation file.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ls/main.go compiles successfully with go build ./cmd/ls/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Running the binary with no arguments lists entries in the current directory\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"The -l flag produces long-format output with permissions, link count, owner, group, size, and modification time\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"The -a flag shows all entries including those starting with dot; -A shows all except . and ..\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Exit code is 0 on success and non-zero when a named operand cannot be accessed\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"No direct imports of golang.org/x/sys in cmd/ls/ -- all syscall access goes through pkg/sys\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"27e2b6c6-29bf-4781-84ca-db8631a7b314","total_cost_usd":0.500718,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19044,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"output_tokens":14946,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19044},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14946,"cacheReadInputTokens":16066,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19044,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.500718,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"3d2db4e5-008c-428f-887c-bd534